<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sovereign yr shr slips, no div.</title>
<headline>Sovereign yr shr slips, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended February, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     20.59	   vs    57.08</p>
<p>    diluted		   20.59	   vs    55.46</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    5.30	   vs    14.27</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    1.35 paid    vs    0.43 received</p>
<p>    Turnover		 127.00	   vs    77.49</p>
<p>Full name: Sovereign Food Investments Ltd (food)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it would not declare a dividend due to the high levels of capital expenditure which were funded out of its own resources. It said the position will be reviewed in August.</p>
<p>Maize prices were expected to decline significantly over the next financial year and would have a positive impact on the broiler business.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
